'''Hallowfall''' is a subterranean [[zone]] in [[Khaz Algar]], located below and to the west of the [[Ringing Deeps]] and north and above [[Azj-Kahet]]. Hallowfall is a landscape of verdant plateaus and river canyons bordered to the west by the endless [[Undersea]], all within an enormous cavern. [[Beledar]], an immense crystal lodged into the cavern ceiling, provides light, warmth, and growth for vegetation, creating a bright and lush environment reminiscent of the surface world. It is inhabited by the [[Hallowfall Arathi]], an expedition of the [[Arathi Empire]]. From their capital of [[Mereldar]], the Arathi use their [[Arathi airship|airships]] to travel throughout the cavern and establish docks, farms, and villages.<ref name="What's Next">{{Ref web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tMDQzaRsVqc|title=<nowiki>BlizzCon | The War Within: What's Next Panel | World of Warcraft</nowiki>|author=World of Warcraft|date=2023-11-03|publisher=YouTube|accessdate=2023-11-05}}</ref><ref name="What's Next Recap">{{Ref web|url=https://worldofwarcraft.blizzard.com/en-us/news/24025827/|title=World of Warcraft®: What’s Next Panel Recap|author=Blizzard Entertainment|date=2023-11-03|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20231104042913/https://worldofwarcraft.blizzard.com/en-us/news/24025827/world-of-warcraft-whats-next-panel-recap|archivedate=2023-11-04}}</ref>

The Arathi settled in the area more than a decade before the events of {{Expac|The War Within}},<ref name="Wenren">[[Wenren Althal#Quotes|Wenren Althal quotes]]</ref> after the [[Emperor of the Arathi|Arathi emperor]] received a vision from the [[Sacred Flame]] of Hallowfall and a source of radiant light, the "Emperor's Vision".<ref name="Beledar">[[Beledar- The Emperor's Vision]]</ref> The Hallowfall Expedition traveled across the [[Storming Sea]] to seek out the vision, until their fleet of airships was enveloped in [[Light]] from the Emperor's Vision and magically transported into Hallowfall. The resulting crash left them stranded and cut off from the Empire. The land in Hallowfall proved fertile, and the survivors settled in the cavern under the light of the Emperor's Vision, the "star" they named Beledar.<ref name="Beledar"/><ref name="Where the Light Touches">[[Where the Light Touches]]</ref><ref name="Spar Day">[[Spar Day]]</ref><ref>[[Izaeh Strongiron#Quotes|Izaeh Strongiron quotes]]</ref> Years later, Hallowfall was shook by the [[Day of Darkness]]—the day [[Sargeras]] plunged [[Sword of Sargeras|his sword]] into [[Azeroth]]<ref>[[Nightwatch]]</ref>—and Beledar began periodically shifting into a [[Void]] state.<ref name="Beledar"/><ref name="Spar Day"/> The Arathi now fight a near-constant battle against [[kobyss]] raiders emerging from the Undersea as well as from swarms of [[nerubian]]s from neighboring Azj-Kahet.<ref name="What's Next"/><ref name="What's Next Recap"/> The Arathi consider Hallowfall to be a holy land, a revelation of the Sacred Flame that it is their duty to protect and cleanse from darkness.<ref name="Beledar"/><ref name="Where the Light Touches"/><ref>[[Shadow Curfew Guidelines]]</ref><ref>[[A Scout's Journal]]</ref>

==Getting there==
Players access Hallowfall via the [[Hallowfall Gate]] in [[Ringing Deeps]] and enter via [[Lothar's Landing]]. From there, players can access [[Azj-Kahet]] via the [[Aegis Wall]] in the southeastern part of the zone, or [[Light's Redoubt]] in the southwest.

