==Notes and trivia==
*All of the flora in Hallowfall is turned toward Beledar, much like plants on the surface following the sun.<ref name="What's Next"/><ref>{{Ref web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lvY166dUD7M&t=710s|title=<nowiki>A New Era of Warcraft Storytelling | The War Within</nowiki>|author=World of Warcraft|publisher=YouTube|date=2024-08-19|accessdate=2024-09-11}}</ref>
*The original version of the official site for {{Expac|The War Within}} erroneously described the Hallowfall Arathi as "a human tribe who have battled against [[nerubian]]s for centuries",<ref>{{Ref web|url=https://thewarwithin.blizzard.com/en-us/|title=World of Warcraft®: The War Within™ - Hallowfall|quote=''Lit by a massive crystal at its center, this bright underground zone is home to the Arathi, a human tribe who have battled against nerubians for centuries.''|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20231116063645/https://thewarwithin.blizzard.com/en-us/|archivedate=2023-11-16}}</ref> rather than a recently-arrived branch of the [[Arathi Empire]]. The description was corrected on November 17, 2023.<ref>{{Ref web|url=https://thewarwithin.blizzard.com/en-us/|title=World of Warcraft®: The War Within™ - Hallowfall|quote=''Lit by a massive crystal at its center, this bright underground zone is home to the Arathi who are engaged in a continuing battle against the nerubians.''|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20231117132902/https://thewarwithin.blizzard.com/en-us/|archivedate=2023-11-17}}</ref>
*During ''The War Within'' beta, [[Wenren Althal]]'s dialogue stated that the Hallowfall Arathi had set out from [[Arathi Empire|the Empire]] fifteen years prior to ''The War Within'',<ref>[[Wenren Althal#Beta version|Wenren Althal beta dialogue]]</ref> while the quest [[Mereldar's Light]] stated that they'd had arrived to Hallowfall ten years prior to ''The War Within''.<ref>[[Mereldar's Light]] - [[Mereldar's Light#Alpha version|Alpha version]]</ref> Prior to release, the former reference was changed to a vaguer "over a decade ago"<ref name="Wenren"/> and the latter was removed entirely.
*Hallowfall appears to be inspired by the {{Wp|Hollow Earth theory|Hollow Earth}} trope commonly seen in {{Wp|subterranean fiction}}. Many Hollow Earth stories portray a lush underground world sustained by an inner sun, often also featuring a subterranean ocean and lost civilizations of ancient humans.

